  "finalAnswerPreview": "## What the object is\\n\\nThe workspace pins four `@ordarium` tarballs to release `ordarium-v1.3.1` (`package.json` dependency block), and the installed artifacts are `@ordarium/core@1.3.1` and `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite@1.3.1`. Inside that pinned artifact there is exactly one surface described as *incremental observation after a durable position* (`ORD-BOOT-0`):\\n\\n- `StateChangeFeed.changes(filter?, cursor?)` → `StateChangePage { changes, cursor, hasMore }` (`core/dist/src/types.d.ts:169,186-191`)\\n- exposed to consumers as `OrdariumStateStore.changes()` (`core/dist/src/state.d.ts:26-30`)\\n\\nThat `StateChangePage.cursor` is the incremental state-observation cursor. Two neighbours in the same artifact are **not** it, and I kept them separate: the `nextCursor?` keyset-pagination cursors (`list`/`history`/`stateHistory`/`listStates`/`listStatesReferencing`), and — outside the dependency entirely — palimpsest's own `graph.project.cursor` / `?cursor=` / `viewCursor`.\\n\\n## Exact semantics (from the pinned artifact)\\n\\n**Position, not payload**\\n- Encoding: base64url of `{\\\"c\\\":\\\"<digits>\\\"}`; strictly validated (`/^\\\\d+$/`, safe integer ≥ 0); anything else throws `InvalidCursorError` (co",
